menu "Weather Glass"

    config GLASS_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Set it in sdkconfig.defaults.local (not tracked) rather than here,
            so the credential does not end up in the repository.

    config GLASS_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default ""

    config GLASS_LATITUDE
        string "Latitude"
        default "12.9698"
        help
            Decimal degrees, south negative. Drives the sun and moon position,
            the star field, day/night and the fetch.

    config GLASS_LONGITUDE
        string "Longitude"
        default "77.7499"

    config GLASS_CITY
        string "City name shown in the header"
        default "Bengaluru"
        help
            Left blank, the header falls back to the city part of the
            timezone Open-Meteo reports.

    config GLASS_TIMEZONE
        string "Open-Meteo timezone"
        default "auto"
        help
            "auto" makes the API pick from the coordinates and return the UTC
            offset it used, which is what the RTC is set from. Pin it to a
            name like Asia/Kolkata if the device sits near a zone boundary.

    config GLASS_UTC_OFFSET_SEC
        int "Fallback UTC offset in seconds (used only when offline)"
        default 19800
        help
            Applied to the RTC when no fetch succeeded, so the clock keeps
            showing sensible local time between refreshes.

    config GLASS_DAY_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "Minutes between fetches while the sun is up"
        default 30
        range 1 1440
        help
            A gap of 15 minutes or more is rounded up to a whole number of
            Open-Meteo's 900 s model steps, so every fetch sees an observation
            that could have changed. Set in config.toml, not here.

    config GLASS_NIGHT_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "Minutes between fetches while the sun is down"
        default 120
        range 1 1440
        help
            Overnight the temperature moves a couple of degrees and nobody is
            looking at the panel, so this can be slow.

    config GLASS_RETRY_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "Minutes before a failed fetch is retried"
        default 5
        range 1 1440
        help
            Not so soon that a dead access point drains the cell in an
            afternoon.

endmenu
